 "notes": [
  "Logistic regression of critical stance (Alarm or Caution) on publication year (continuous, centred on 2023.856), genre, publication type, specialty and first-author region; n=14,058; events=4283; 2278 journal clusters; cluster-robust (journal) SEs. Logistic regression of Advocacy vs not; n=14,058; events=218; 2278 journal clusters; levels with fewer than 5 Advocacy events collapsed into 'Other (<5 events)'. Proportional-odds logistic model (Alarm < Caution < Neutral < Cautious Optimism < Advocacy); OR > 1 = more favourable; n=14,058; cluster-robust SEs; cut-point ORs from separate binary models. Proportional odds was judged violated when a cut-point coefficient fell outside the ordinal coefficient's CI or changed sign; fails for 27 of 32 terms (pre-specified rule), mainly at the Advocacy cut point. S1: year as categories (reference 2021). S2: adds January-April 2026 as a year level (n=16,747; the only model that uses 2026 records). S3: journal fixed effects (n=8529 records, 2728 events, 275 journals). S4: first-author country levels with at least 100 records (reference United States) instead of region. Reference levels and covariates as in Table 2. All SEs cluster-robust by journal."
 ],
